ESP32 PayBot is a simple and low-cost approach to creating a payment voice alert system. 
Instead of directly integrating the ESP32 with a payment service or requiring a dedicated
merchant account, the system uses the payment notification already generated on a smartphone. 

This makes the setup easier for small shops, students, and DIY projects while still providing an instant 
voice announcement of the received amount.
When a payment is received, the payment app sends a notification to the phone. MacroDroid
detects this notification and forwards its contents to the Blynk server using MQTT. 

The ESP32 receives the notification data from Blynk, identifies the payment amount, and 
converts it into a voice announcement. The voice signal is sent through the PAM8403 amplifier to the speaker, 
allowing the PayBot to announce the received amount automatically.

